  nonce: '9e25'  # 9e25
  message: "DEFERRED (demand-gated) in the G8 sweep. config_fingerprint (ir.py) keys on producer identity and does NOT distinguish same-pass runs under different runtime CLI flags (--include-docs/--max-tier/frameworks/file-lang filters) — the invariant IS violated. But it has NO internal consumer (external cache-keying only, ir.py:267-274), and the fix is a SEMANTIC REDEFINITION (identity -> runtime-config) that also perturbs the finalize run_signature recompute. Per the item's own re-eval trigger and the hypergumbo-spirit 'no complexity without a consumer' call, do NOT redefine config_fingerprint until a consumer needs same-pass/different-flag distinction. Left violated (honest) + this note; reopen when a cache-distinction consumer appears. This does not need human input — it's a deliberate scope call. G8 now COMPLETE: WI-pifaj #7, WI-fonod/WI-givad #12, WI-sijug #13 done; INV-nogom demand-gated-deferred."  # 9e25
